# First Duplicate (First Number Encountered Twice)

## Pattern
HashMap / Set

## Recognition
- Find the first duplicate
- First repeated element
- Return the first element encountered twice

## Approach
- Create an empty set.
- Iterate through the array.
- If the current number is already in the set, return it.
- Otherwise, add it to the set.
- If no duplicate exists, return `None`.

## Code

```python
def first_duplicate(nums):
    seen = set()

    for num in nums:
        if num in seen:
            return num
        seen.add(num)

    return None
```

## Complexity

Time: O(n)

Space: O(n)

## Interview Tip

"I'll use a set because I only need to know whether I've seen an element before. A set provides O(1) average lookup, making the overall solution O(n)."

## Common Mistakes
❌ Using a dictionary when only existence is needed.

❌ Returning all duplicates instead of the first repeated one.

❌ Confusing "first duplicate encountered" with "first element having frequency > 1".